MODULE NavigatorOptions;

REQUIRE TestUtils;

// a navigator element keeps the options statements give it (NAVIGATOR { element WINDOW ... IMAGE ... CHANGEKEY ... }),
// some of them in pairs : a window and whether it is the parent's, an image and the property computing it, a key and
// whether it is shown. Modules that do not require each other are parsed at once, each in a thread of its own, so two of
// them that set one element up wrote the pairs at once : a lab start of eight such modules left the element with the
// window of one and the PARENT of another. And which of two statements an option kept was the one written last, so the
// parse threads' timing : the options are NF at the module's version now, so the later module's win, as when the modules
// were parsed one after the other, a pair from one statement. The NF writes take no lock of the element

noEarlierImage () = 'earlier';
noLaterImage () = 'later';

noOrderFailure = DATA LOCAL STRING ();
noSetInModuleOrder INTERNAL 'lsfusion.tests.SetNavigatorOptionsInModuleOrderAction' ();

testNavigatorOptionsInModuleOrder 'Of two modules setting options of a navigator element the later one in the module order wins' () {
    noSetInModuleOrder();
    assertNull(noOrderFailure(), noOrderFailure());
}
